    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d304">

                <pb facs="0347" n="271" xml:id="pg271"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 351.117/62</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Sharp to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 19, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1224. Your 1317, January 15. French Government’s decision reported fully in
                    despatch 1853, January 11. Kirghis stated to Embassy that he was warned by
                    authorities in United States before sailing that he would be liable to military
                    service in France. Records of Embassy tend to show that French Government, even
                    in time of peace, has not departed from custom of requiring military service
                    from those persons subject to it by French law notwithstanding naturalization of
                    such persons. All requests based on similar circumstances presented by this
                    Embassy since beginning of war have been refused. Believe further
                    representations on behalf of Kirghis would be fruitless. Please instruct whether
                    you desire additional action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
